Content-Type: text/plain;
	charset="iso-8859-1"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Ok...got lots of responses right away.  The golden command is "ulimit =
-a" (while logged in as the user in question).  doing this I noticed =
this user's "data" was set much much lower to the user with no problems. =
 So all I had to do was add the "ulimit -d <limit>" line to the users =
.profile and everything is great now.  Thanks much to Kurt Ludwig, David =
DeWolfe, Keith Strange, Selden Ball, and Peyton Bland for their =
responses.

Jonathan Williams
UNIX Systems Administrator
The Shubert Organization, Inc.

