From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Jul 31 13:43:03 2001
From: Paul Reilly <pareilly () tcd ! ie>
Date: Tue, 31 Jul 2001 13:43:03 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Samba - replacing passwd command?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653652422146


Hi,

Has anyone got a good way of keeping the Samba password file in sync with
the UNIX password file ? I need to get the users to run smbclient at the
same time as passwd, but of course they are not going to do this. I was thinking of
replacing the /usr/bin/passwd command with a wrapper that calls both
programs? This would work, but I think it may cause other problems if
/usr/bin/passwd isn't the real passwd program (for instance does sysman
use this command, or does it access the library functions directly?)

Any advice on how others have solved this problem, or any ideas if the
above soln would cause problem would be appreciated,

Paul

From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Jul 31 13:26:03 2001
From: cknorr <cknorr () hops ! com>
Date: Tue, 31 Jul 2001 13:26:03 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Pointer to StorageWorks Command Console Software
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653652422145

Thanks to Dela Acolatse, Dan Price, and Blake Brehl for their replies, as 
well as a late-breaking reply from Robert Aldridge. The StorageWorks 
Command Console v2.1 can be found at:

http://www.compaq.com/products/storageworks/storage-management-software/swccdownload.html#swcc

However the latest version doesn't seem to be available on the web. Dan 
indicated that delivery of the SWCC software to a customer is considered a 
'chargeable deliverable'. It's unclear to me if this explains why v2.3 
isn't available on the web. Robert indicated they're not going to put this 
software out on the web anymore. Bummer if true, which seems likely.

Dela indicated she'd received the software on a CD with her ES40 and, since 
I'd just gotten one of these puppies I checked and, sure enough, I had the 
necessary CD.

Just as an FYI, the CD that contains the software is labeled:

Compaq StorageWorks
RA7000/ESA10000
Solution Software V7.7A
for Compaq Tru64 Unix		April 2000

and the actual software agent to install is called

SWCC500.TAR

Rather confusing, but both represent the pathway to the SWCC v2.3 Tru64 
Unix agent.

Chris

