From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Jul 31 10:07:22 2001
From: Jason Smith <jsmith165 () email ! com>
Date: Tue, 31 Jul 2001 10:07:22 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: DU4.0F/TCR1.6 Patch Kit upgrade
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653652422142

Original Question:

> I have a 3 node Digital UNIX 4.0F TCR1.6 ASE cluster running Patch Kit 
> 4 and want to upgrade it to Patch Kit 6. 
> 
> Is it sufficient to fail over the services off one of the nodes, 
> install the patch kit as you would for a non clustered system, then 
> repeat the process on the other 2 nodes? 
> 
> Is it necessary to delete the nodes from the cluster using asemgr? 
> 
> The patch installation guide seems to be general for DU4.0 and Tru64 
> 5.x. It mentions rolling upgrades but that seems to be for V5 
> clusters. 



Thanks to Dr. Thomas P. Blinn for the following answer

You're right, the rolling upgrades are a V5.x TruCluster Server feature. 

For your older V4.x ASE cluster, the method you describe should just work, unless the patch documentation explicitly describes something else as the right method. With the older ASE clusters, the cluster nodes are really quite independent of one another and almost all of the "smarts" is in the failover services (ASE manager). As long as you have shown in the past that things fail over if you shut a system down and leave it down for some time (e.g., to do stand-alone backups or the like or to do hardware maintenance), you should be golden. Unless the patch kit explicitly says you have to "uncluster" the systems and then re-make the cluster after the patching, you should just be able to update each 
member one at a time as you describe. 



