From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Jul 27 02:40:23 2001
From: Raymond Pang <wmpang () se ! cuhk ! edu ! hk>
Date: Fri, 27 Jul 2001 02:40:23 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Can a high R/W NFS service be relocated in TruCluster 5.1?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653652422092

Hi Managers,

"cfsmgr -a statistics" shows that high R/W NFS services are unevenly 
distributed in the two-member TruCluster (5.1). For example, three high R/W
NFS services are on server A and only one is on server B. In TCR 1.5, you 
can use asemgr to relocate the NFS service to another server. 

Manual only says that it is better to relocate the server to the member 
that is serving the service with most of the R/W activity. But if
unfortunately most of the high R/W NFS services are on one server, say
after the reboot of one member. How can I force some out of that high 
loading server?

Thanks and regards,
Raymond

