sunguide1 [/] #

Answer:

I think the command you want is:


# net helpmsg 6550

The required UNIX account '***' is not present.



I don't know if this is as a result of bad account mappings (mapuname may
give you a clue). If you've never got ASU to run I'd start from scratch.
Delete the software, remove any associated accounts and try again.
Having just run mapuname on my server on my desk I saw initially a load of
remnants from a previous config though "mapuname -p" has cleared this out.

Solution

I finally solved the problem performing setld -d ASUADM502 ASUMANPAGE502 
etc..... include all the modules that start with word ASU.
Then I re-install ASU, but during the asusetup I used a different Admin. 
password (previously I was using the same password as root have), and I 
let all the default assumptions as they where selected by the setup 
program. Later on I stopped the server ' net stop server' and ran 
asusetup again to adjust my desire settings like domain name.I think 
that the problem was solved when I used a different admin. password 
because I tried several times to uninstall and reinstall ASU following 
the same steps without success, The last installation of ASU I tried a different password , and BOON!! 

it started the server at the end .
