From: "Hill, NM \(Nick\) " <N.M.Hill () rl ! ac ! uk>
Date: Wed, 18 Jul 2001 16:07:09 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Boot after install problem
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653652421934


Original question: 

> Bootstrap address collision, image loading aborted

As I had suspected this was a console version issue. The firmware version
was several versions ahead of what V5.0 originally shipped with. 

As Dr Thomas P. Blinn from COMPAQ said:

The firmware grew in later versions, and there was work done in the
kernel build procedures to be able to deal with it; I suspect that
you have newer firmware that needs the new kernel features that were
not in the old release.

Edward Ady from COMPAQ provided the solution:

There is a console variable that you can set to alleviate this problem:

>>> set console_memory_allocation old
Power cycle machine.

Which fixed the problem.

