Thank you to all who responded.
 
The consensus is that the directory cannot be deleted.  It seems that Tru64
uses this for future patch releases to possibly back out some patches as a
precondition (among other things).  One suggestion was to create a link to
another drive with more space.  I am taking all into consideration.
 
Thanks again.
 
Dawn Urey 
 
-----Original Message-----
From: Urey, Dawn [mailto:UreyD@pginw.com]
Sent: Tuesday, July 17, 2001 10:39 AM
To: Tru64 Managers (E-mail)
Subject: /var/adm/patch
 
All:
I understand that after applying a patch to the system, some information
gets put in /var/adm/patch.  I a directory called /var/adm/patch/backup
which, I am thinking, was put there because I wanted the ability to back out
the patch should anything happen.  My system has been running perfectly fine
and I am not intending to back this patch out.  My question is this:  Is it
ok to delete those files?  I am running short of space and these files take
up quite a bit of it.
Thanks,
Dawn Urey
System Admin 
