<P><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Admins,</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Basically I have a system image on =
another machine and I'm copying it over via FTP.&nbsp; I've booted from =
the cd-rom, set up the file domains, filesets, mount points, from a =
newly created disklabel and when I try to copy the /usr fileset over =
(like a 600 mb tgz file) I get the following error.&nbsp; </FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Hard Error Detected</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">SEAGATE ST39236LW</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Active CCB at time of error</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">CCB request completed with an =
error</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Error, exception, or abnormal =
command</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">ABORTED COMMAND - TARGET ABORTED =
COMMAND</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">AdvFS I/O error:</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Domain #Fileset: usr_domain#usr</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Mounted on: /var/tmp/mnt/usr</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Volume: /dev/rz0g</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Tag: 0x00000007.8003</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Page: 57462</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Block: 8588416</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Block count: 128</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Type of operator: Write</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Error: 5</FONT>
</P>
<BR>

<P><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">I have tried to re-create the error on =
another machine but have had no luck - it seems to copy just ine.&nbsp; =
I would assume that the disk has bad sectors but we all not what =
assumptions do.&nbsp; Please help!!</FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">Thanks in advance,</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Times New Roman">Brandon Malli</FONT>

