From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Jul 13 08:23:41 2001
From: Emilio Sergi <e.sergi () somacis ! com>
Date: Fri, 13 Jul 2001 08:23:41 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Problem with Alpha Workstation and Cisco Switch
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653652421847

The autonegotiation of speed and duplex between the workstation's Ethernet
card and the Cisco router is the source of the problem.
The solution: force the the settings of router and the workstation to 100MB
FullDuplex and don't use the autonegotiation.
At the OS level (Tru64):

  # lan_config -i tu0 -s 100 -x 1

At the SRM level:

>>> set ewa0_mode FastFD

Thanks to all.

Emilio.

