Alright.  I feel proud.  I actually figured out the problems without =
reading any of the MANY replies I received.  After reading the replies I =
find that just about everyone said the same thing.  A misconfigured =
network.  Actually, the network was configured nicely...it's just that =
there are no active network connections to the server yet!!  I knew that =
ahead of time, I just didn't realize Unix really REALLY  doesn't like =
not being hooked up to the network it was set up for.  What I had to do =
was go back into failsafe mode, and remove any trace of network =
settings--mostly just the /etc/hosts file had to be emptied of =
everything but the localhost 127.0.0.1 line.  And now it works just =
great.  Thanks to everyone who replied.  =3D)  Bye

Jonathan Williams
