To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Will advFS disks be readable when downgrading from
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653652421711

Thanks to Kevin Partin, Corinne Haesaerts, and Chris Ruhnke for their quick 
responses! This from Kevin:

If you created your AdvFS domains in Tru64 UNIX v5, then you will have to 
recreate your AdvFS domains and file sets once you have installed Tru64 
UNIX v4.0, and then restore your data from tape. Tru64 UNIX v5 uses AdvFS 
version 4. Tru64 UNIX v4 uses AdvFS version 3. While Tru64 UNIX v5 can read 
and write to domains created using Tru64 UNIX v4, the opposite is not true. 
You can verify your AdvFS domain version using the showfdmn command. The 
output of the command will list the version of the domain. In Tru64 UNIX 
v5, the version number is four.

Chris

