Original post

Hi,

When I run scu show edt, parts of the output show

    Device: DATA ROUTER Bus: 6, Target: 4, Lun: 0, Type: Array Controller
    Device: TZ89       Bus: 6, Target: 4, Lun: 5, Type: Sequential Access
    Device: TZ89       Bus: 6, Target: 4, Lun: 6, Type: Sequential Access
=20

When I trry MAKEDEV tzf52, it can not create the device with the following =
error:

# ./MAKEDEV tzf52
MAKEDEV: special file(s) for tzf52:=20
MAKEDEV: unknown device in: tzf52


Solution:

Sorry for being late and thanks to all who responded especially Alan who =
pointed out that MAKEDEV does not create non-zero LUN tape devices and I =
am attaching his reply for completeness.  In the end, I had to do what =
Alan suggested and created the devices using mknod using the following =
formula and all now work:

(LUN x 64) + (Target ID x 1024) + (Bus # x 16384) + (Density x 2) + rewind

where
rewind =3D 0
no_rewind =3D 1

Density:

	low  =3D (0x2)
	high =3D (1x2)
	med  =3D (2x2)
	aux  =3D (3x2)


Regards,
Hoai Tran



